    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d125-a1">

                <pb facs="0136" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg130"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Press telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The Bering Sea Fisheries</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Victoria, British Columbia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                25</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The British Columbia sealing catch, including the take of two American vessels,
                    amounts to 70,000 skins. Many of the schooners will go to Japan next season,
                    about half their number setting out before Christmas. It is stated that some of
                    these vessels are likely to transfer their allegiance to another flag.</p>
            </div>
